{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The British University Hurling Championship is an annual Hurling competition held for universities in Great Britain.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is organised by the BUGAA which is a branch of the Higher Education GAA committee which oversees Gaelic Games in Universities.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Unlike its sister competition, the British University Gaelic Football Championship, this competition is not overseen by the British Universities Sports Association as yet.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The best players each year are chosen for an all-star team to play the Scottish Universities Shinty Team.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The trophies for British University Gaelic Games Championships memorialise students who were pioneers of Gaelic Games at British Universities.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The Michael O'Leary Cup is awarded to the winner of the British University Hurling Championship.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It was presented to BUGAA by The Friary, Dundee.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The Cup is named after a founder member of the hurling club at the University of Glasgow who died in 2001.","title":"British University Hurling Championship"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Katherine Murray Millett (September 14, 1934 – September 6, 2017) was an American feminist writer, educator, artist, and activist.","title":"Kate Millett"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She attended Oxford University and was the first American woman to be awarded a degree with first-class honors after studying at St Hilda's College, Oxford.","title":"Kate Millett"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She has been described as "a seminal influence on second-wave feminism", and is best known for her book "Sexual Politics" (1970), which was based on her doctoral dissertation at Columbia University.","title":"Kate Millett"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Journalist Liza Featherstone attributes previously unimaginable "legal abortion, greater professional equality between the sexes, and a sexual freedom" being made possible partially due to Millett's efforts.","title":"Kate Millett"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Contract With the World is a 1980 novel written by Canadian author Jane Rule.","title":"Contract with the World"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The story takes place in Vancouver, British Columbia, in the mid-1970s, and is divided in six parts, each focusing on the perspective of a different character.","title":"Contract with the World"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Themes of artistic motivation, personal fulfilment, and sexual politics are present throughout.","title":"Contract with the World"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Au Pairs were a British post-punk band that formed in Birmingham in 1978 and continued until 1983.","title":"Au Pairs (band)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" They produced two studio albums and three singles.","title":"Au Pairs (band)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Their songs were said to have "contempt for the cliches of contemporary sexual politics" and their music has been compared to the Gang of Four and the Young Marble Giants.","title":"Au Pairs (band)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The band was led by Lesley Woods, who was once described as "one of the most striking women in British rock".","title":"Au Pairs (band)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Susannah "Susie" Bright, also known as Susie Sexpert (born March 25, 1958), is an American feminist, author, journalist, critic, editor, publisher, producer, and performer, often on the subject of sexual politics and sexuality.","title":"Susie Bright"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Carol J. Adams (born 1951) is an American writer, feminist, and animal rights advocate.","title":"Carol J. Adams"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is the author of several books, including "The Sexual Politics of Meat: A Feminist-Vegetarian Critical Theory" (1990) and "The Pornography of Meat" (2004), focusing in particular on what she argues are the links between the oppression of women and that of non-human animals.","title":"Carol J. Adams"}],"peer_messages":[" which was based on her doctoral dissertation at Columbia University.","title":"Kate Millett"}
