{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Handheld camera, shaky cam, queasy cam, queasicam, hand-held camera or free camera is a cinematographic technique where stable-image techniques are purposely dispensed with.","title":"Shaky camera"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The camera is held in the hand, or given the appearance of being hand-held, and in many cases shots are limited to what one photographer could have accomplished with one camera.","title":"Shaky camera"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Shaky cam is often employed to give a film sequence an ad hoc, electronic news-gathering, or documentary film feel.","title":"Shaky camera"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It suggests unprepared, unrehearsed filming of reality, and can provide a sense of dynamics, immersion, instability or nervousness.","title":"Shaky camera"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The technique can be used to give a pseudo-documentary or "cinéma vérité" appearance to a film.","title":"Shaky camera"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cameron Arthur "Cam" Clarke (born November 6, 1957) is an American voice actor and singer, known for his voice-work in animation and video games.","title":"Cam Clarke"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is best known for providing the voices of Leonardo and Rocksteady in the original "Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles" animated series and Shotaro Kaneda in the 1989 original English dub of "Akira".","title":"Cam Clarke"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He often voices teenagers and other similarly young characters.","title":"Cam Clarke"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" One of his prominent roles in video games was voicing Liquid Snake in the "Metal Gear" series.","title":"Cam Clarke"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"John Clarke, CM (February 25, 1945 – January 23, 2003) was a Canadian explorer, mountaineer, conservationist, and wilderness educator.","title":"John Clarke (mountaineer)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was born in Ireland to Brigit Ann Clarke (née Conway) and Thomas Kevin Clarke, and died in Vancouver, British Columbia of a brain tumor.","title":"John Clarke (mountaineer)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" From 1964 until his death in 2003 Clarke spent at least six months of each year on extended backcountry trips, usually into the Coast Mountains of British Columbia using the technique of dropping food caches from small planes along an intended route, then traveling that route for weeks at a time.","title":"John Clarke (mountaineer)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" His routes regularly led him along the high ridges and glaciated icefields of the west coast, and allowed him to make hundreds of first ascents of the many mountains along the way.","title":"John Clarke (mountaineer)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Many of these trips exceeded 30 days in length, and were often done solo, simply because nobody could afford the time to accompany him.","title":"John Clarke (mountaineer)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Akira (あきら, アキラ ) is a common Japanese given name.","title":"Akira (given name)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" There are several kanji for Akira.","title":"Akira (given name)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" A popular kanji is 明 which means "bright", "intelligent", or "clear".","title":"Akira (given name)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Though Akira is normally used to name males, it can be a female name as well.","title":"Akira (given name)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Transfer is a technique used in propaganda and advertising.","title":"Transfer (propaganda)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Also known as association, this is a technique of projecting positive or negative qualities (praise or blame) of a person, entity, object, or value (an individual, group, organization, nation, patriotism, etc.) to another in order to make the second more acceptable or to discredit it.","title":"Transfer (propaganda)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It evokes an emotional response, which stimulates the target to identify with recognized authorities.","title":"Transfer (propaganda)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Often highly visual, this technique often utilizes symbols superimposed over other visual images.","title":"Transfer (propaganda)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" An example of common use of this technique in the United States is for the President to be filmed or photographed in front of the country's flag.","title":"Transfer (propaganda)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Another technique used is celebrity endorsement.","title":"Transfer (propaganda)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Common Area Maintenance charges, or CAM for short, are one of the net charges billed to tenants in a commercial triple net (NNN) lease, and are paid by tenants to the landlord of a commercial property.","title":"Common area maintenance charges"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" A CAM charge is an additional rent, charged on top of base rent, and is mainly composed of maintenance fees for work performed on the common area of a property.","title":"Common area maintenance charges"}],"peer_messages":["Cameron Arthur \"Cam\" Clarke (born November 6, 1957) is an American voice actor and singer, known for his voice-work in animation and video games.","title":"Cam Clarke"}
