ball"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" The Rams have also won the Lone Star Conference tournament championship two times, including the 2015 LSC Championship when the team swept their way to the title and in 2012.","title":"Angelo State Rams baseball"},{"sentence_id":11,"text":" His list of accomplishments includes the LSC South Division title in 2006, the Lone Star Conference and NCAA Division II South Central Regional titles in 2007,2015, and 2016, a semifinal appearance in the 2009 South Central Regional tournament and the LSC regular season and tournament championships in 2012.","title":"Angelo State Rams baseball"},{"sentence_id":12,"text":" He has coached over 100 All-Lone Star Conference selections, 40 All-Region picks and 23 All-American selections.","title":"Angelo State Rams baseball"},{"sentence_id":13,"text":" Brooks has also prepared his players for the next level as 22 former Rams have played or are currently playing professional baseball, including 7 in the last 2 years.","title":"Angelo State Rams baseball"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Kent State Golden Flashes women's basketball team represents Kent State University in Kent, Ohio, United States.","title":"Kent State Golden Flashes women's basketball"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The Golden Flashes compete in the Mid-American Conference East Division and last played in the NCAA Division I Women's Basketball Tournament in 2002.","title":"Kent State Golden Flashes women's basketball"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Founded in 1973 as a club team, the Kent State women's basketball team received varsity status in 1975 and played their first official game in January 1976.","title":"Kent State Golden Flashes women's basketball"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Through the 2016–17 season, the Flashes have five total appearances in the NCAA Division I women's basketball tournament along with three Mid-American Conference tournament championships, five MAC overall titles, and eight MAC East division titles.","title":"Kent Sta